{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nOperator decisions supersede this ticket's original framing (see its comments). **2026-08-10:** do\nNOT retune the fuzzy `low|medium|high` boundary — ordinal labels are an LLM anti-pattern, since\nmodels do not apply them reliably enough for deterministic gate behavior; replace each ladder with a\nclosed KIND set mapping deterministically to floor-vs-advisory in code. **2026-08-12:** do both\nhalves now — drop the inert-G5 hedge (no bump) AND land the conversion under its own\n`IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump (plan-v5). Per the **C11 plan**\n(`reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/ordinal-migration-plan.md` Phase 1) the plan-v5 batch is both\naxes plus the no-bump margin rider.\n\nEvidence, from this checkout's persisted REVIEW_RESULT sidecar corpus (22,503 plan findings carrying\n`verification.severity_attributes`). Every non-none grade on both axes floors impact to 0.85\n(`_PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_FLOOR` in `decide.py`), so `low` == `high`. Of `undecomposed`'s 30 graded\nbodies, 21 are \"this plan bundles N independently-releasable outcomes\" — a right-sizing observation\non an otherwise executable plan — yet each floors and 4 blocked. `dod_uncertifiable` is graded 1,413\ntimes, mixing three distinct defects under one blind floor. Both prompts and the `undecomposed`\ndescription justify conservatism by citing the deterministic G5 suppressor, but\n`veto_undecomposed_g5` fired ZERO times, so that hedge is inert. `ORACLE_GRADE01` (v3) and\n`DIVERGENCE_GRADE01` (v4) are the precedents.\n\n## What\n\n**Scope is ONE unit, not a bundle to split.** ADR 0054 section 4 requires impact-model shape changes\nto be batched behind one `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump, since each bump closes the current cohort.\nItems 2-3 are shape changes; 1 and 4 are no-bump riders that would otherwise be stranded from their\nevidence. NOT independently releasable.\n\n1. **Prompt rewrite (no bump).** Delete the inert G5-suppressor hedge from both prompts and the\n   `undecomposed` description in `verify_models.py`. Both prompts' bullets for these two axes are\n   also REWRITTEN (see Steps) to enumerate the six new kinds and their pick-this-kind rules.\n\n2. **`undecomposed` -> closed kind set (bump):** `none`; `bundles_separable_slices` — executable as\n   written but packs outcomes that could each ship alone, so splitting only improves clarity —\n   contributing `UNDECOMPOSED_BUNDLED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `missing_required_child` —\n   work the plan or its parent commits to has NO child/sibling — flooring;\n   `no_executable_breakdown` — no executable step sequence for its scope, or an all-or-nothing\n   build whose riskiest unknown is never de-risked first — flooring.\n3. **`dod_uncertifiable` -> closed kind set (bump):** `none`; `underspecified_certification` — the\n   outcome IS certifiable and an oracle exists, but its exact command/path/assertion is not spelled\n   out — contributing `DOD_UNDERSPECIFIED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `uncertifiable_outcome` —\n   a committed outcome has NO acceptance criterion, test or proving mechanism — flooring;\n   `certification_cannot_prove` — a stated mechanism cannot establish the outcome (it names\n   something that does not exist or cannot detect what is claimed, or a trivially broken\n   implementation satisfies it) — flooring.\n4. **Decision-margin telemetry (no bump).** Record `priority - block_threshold` per finding in the\n   sidecar (C11 P0.2 — that plan says `impact_sev`, but `pass3_decide` blocks on\n   `priority >= block_threshold` with `priority = validity x impact`, so the margin must use\n   `priority` to reflect the real boundary). Additive only.\n5. **Bump `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` plan-v4 -> plan-v5** in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`.\n\n**Evidence gate before landing (zero LLM).** Add\n`reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/plan_v5_rescore.py` re-scoring all 22,503 recorded findings\nunder the new maps and reporting old-vs-new flips; land rules and output under `docs/calibration/`.\nIt reads persisted `severity_attributes` as RAW dicts (never through the new `Literal` model, which\nrejects the old labels), mapping each grade to a kind by documented rules. Per the R1 bar, a lost\nblock is UNJUSTIFIED iff the finding body describes a genuine gap (a committed outcome with\nno/broken oracle, or missing required decomposition) yet re-maps to an advisory kind; any such flip\nmeans ESCALATE with the data, not land.\n\n## Steps\n\nImplement items 1-5 above in order, then 6-7 below.\n\n`_SEV01` maps only `none|low|medium|high`, returning 0.0 for any kind name. `impact_plan` reads\nthese axes through `_SEV01` in THREE places, and ALL THREE must be rewritten against the new\n`*_GRADE01` maps or the axes silently go dead: the contribs MAX (via `_PLAN_SEVERITY_AXES`), the\n`has_override` floor loop (via `_PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_AXES`), and the `dod_uncertifiable` amplifier\nforce of `mult = 1.0`. Adding both axes to `_PLAN_GRADED_AXES` excludes them from the first two\nloops; the amplifier force is a separate rewrite.\n\nThe verifier EMITS these values, so both prompts' `undecomposed` / `dod_uncertifiable` bullets are\nREWRITTEN to enumerate all six kinds with their pick-this-kind rules and advisory-vs-flooring\nsemantics — not just the `verify_models.py` `Field` text — matching the existing\n`divergent_implementation` bullet's form.\n\n6. In `tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py` REWRITE (not merely extend) the pre-existing ordinal-keyed\n   cases for these axes — `test_hard_override_floors_low_axis_to_085`,\n   `test_each_ordinal_override_axis_triggers_floor`,\n   `test_dod_uncertifiable_forces_full_detection_weight` — to kind names, then add the new cases;\n   update `tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py`; pin the margin in\n   `tests/unit/test_plan_review_sidecar.py`. `test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py` pins the\n   \"success criterion\" phrasing in the `dod_uncertifiable` bullet, so PRESERVE it.\n7. Write the re-score script; record rules + results in `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both axes are closed `Literal` kind sets. Verified: `python -m pytest\n      tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q -k literal` passes, asserting each field's annotation holds\n      the six kind names and none of `low`/`medium`/`high`.\n- [ ] Each advisory kind contributes 0.55 and never floors; each gap kind yields 0.85; both CONTRIB\n      constants sit strictly below the lowest blocking `block_threshold` (0.6) in\n      `plan_review/criteria_routing.json`, like `UNDERSPECIFIED_ORACLE_CONTRIB`; the amplifier\n      still forces `mult = 1.0` for a non-none `dod_uncertifiable`. Verified:\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q` passes with cases pinning\n      `impact_plan({\"undecomposed\": \"bundles_separable_slices\"}) == 0.55`, the same for\n      `underspecified_certification`, 0.85 for the four gap kinds, the contrib invariant, and a\n      `self_revealing` + `underspecified_certification` finding at 0.55 not 0.44.\n- [ ] No prompt or description cites the G5 suppressor. Verified:\n      `rg -n \"deterministic G5 signal already|signal already suppresses\" src/rebar/` exits 1.\n- [ ] The sidecar records a per-finding `priority - block_threshold` margin. Verified: `python -m\n      pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_sidecar.py -q -k margin` passes.\n- [ ] `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` is `plan-v5`, batched per ADR 0054 section 4. Verified:\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py -q` passes, and the commit body\n      names the hedge removal, both conversions and the margin telemetry as riding one bump.\n- [ ] The re-score is landed and shows no unjustified lost blocks (rule above). Verified:\n      `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md` states the mapping rules and reports old-vs-new block\n      counts and the flip set; `python\n      reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/plan_v5_rescore.py` reproduces them.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n`veto_undecomposed_g5` removal and C11 Phase 2 (plan-v6). Gates: `make lint && make typecheck` plus\nthe AC pytest commands and `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q -k plan_review`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786510666260985001,"uuid":"eb972b03-f422-44aa-98db-6a7b80cdac31"}